-- title:
--   Centre of the exceptional valuation is yB on the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, and assume some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, algebraically closed residue field, $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$; let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = qu$ with $u$ a unit. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image of the $j$-series over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` be the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing $\varpi$ such that, for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic curves over $\Omega$ have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Let $J \subseteq C$ be an ideal and let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by adjoining to $C$ all $x$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$, and let $W \subseteq K$ be a valuation subring containing $B$. Assume: (R1) $C \subseteq B$ and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$; (R2) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most one; (R3) $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, $\mathfrak m_W = (\varpi)$, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, $W$ is centred on $y$ in the sense that $b \in y \iff b \in \mathfrak m_W$ for $b \in C$, and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W \cap B$. Assume finally that the ideal $yB$ of $B$ generated by the image of $y$ is prime. Then, first, for $b \in B$ one has $b \in \mathfrak m_W$ if and only if $b \in yB$; and second, for every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ whose contraction to $C$ is $y$, every element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ lies in $Q$.
--
--   The statement identifies the centre $\mathfrak m_W \cap B$ of the exceptional valuation ring $W$ on the blow-up chart $B$ with the ideal $yB$ generated by the supersingular point $y$, and shows it to be the least prime of $B$ above $\varpi$ contracting to $y$. It is the form in which the hypotheses of the downstream decomposition- and inertia-group computations at the Drinfeld fibre of the auxiliary level structure are verified, in the variant frame with auxiliary level $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ for a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, which covers the small primes $q$.
